        "reason": "Downstream SQL-on-FHIR consumers join derived tables on getResourceKey() resource keys, which the port computes internally but drops at the outermost SELECT. The attempt adds the paired key column beside each MIMIC identifier column (subject_id->patient_key, hadm_id->encounter_key, stay_id->icu_encounter_key, specimen_id->specimen_key). Additive and shape-only: both comparison paths project manifest columns explicitly, so no compared value can change. The MIMIC integer columns are retained as the oracle join keys.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "human",
        "superseded_error": null,
        "superseded_justification": "Inherited divergence with no charlson-originated loss. All 61/431,231 (0.0141%)   differing_conflict rows fall on age_score and charlson_comorbidity_index and are a   strict subset of the 460 age rows already accepted as COMPLETED_WITH_DIVERGENCE by   human decision. Root cause is upstream: mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_patient.sql:15 synthesises   Patient.birthDate as MIN(transfers.intime)-anchor_age, so FHIR-side age reduces to   anchor_age + year(admittime) - year(MIN(transfers.intime)), diverging from canonical   age.sql:30 exactly where year(MIN(transfers.intime)) != anchor_year. anchor_year is   carried by no FHIR element or extension and is not a function of any published   timestamp: six candidate identities swept, none exact; subject 12047822 has an   admission in 2163 with anchor_year 2165, ruling out first-event-year. 0 only_oracle,   0 only_candidate, 0 differing_null_only; keys, grain, schema and all diagnosis flags   exact at 431,170/431,231 (99.9859%). Reported upstream as mimic-fhir   debug-patient-birthdate-anchor. Recorded against attempt_0002 by human decision, overturning the equivalence judge's BLOCKED_REPRESENTATION ruling on that attempt (attempt_0002/evidence/equivalence-judge.md; metrics/charlson/run_0002.json finalized on that ruling and is write-once). The reopen that followed the block opened attempt_0003, which produced no artifacts and was removed; it is not recorded in reopen_history.",
